{"objective":"Move the EKA standard from prose an agent may ignore into mechanisms a repository enforces: a generated entry point that cannot go stale, a deterministic knowledge-to-path binding, a gate at the agent boundary, and a retrieval surface that is bounded rather than grown. The target state is that an agent working in an EKA repository always holds the Discovery and Architecture strata — especially the standard token family — because the repository refuses work that contradicts them and names the constraint id in the refusal, not because a file asked it to remember.","scope":"Seven work items, ordered so that the ones needing no specification decision land first. M0 (sto:agents-md-generated) — the entry point becomes generated from the repository's own knowledge and drift-checked, so a stale entry point is a failure rather than silence. M3a (sto:verify-changed-gate) — eka verify --changed runs the checks a standard declares against the changed files, installed at the git hook and CI, reporting violations as test failures carrying the constraint id and location. M5 (sto:compliance-telemetry) — the derived compliance signals the capture layer already has the substrate for, aggregated per repository, so M2 versus M3a can be compared with numbers. M1 (sto:knowledge-path-binding) — the only specification change: std-/spec-/adr- declare the paths they bind and eka context --for \u003cpath\u003e returns the constraint set deterministically; inherits standard 1.5, because 1.4 is spent. M2 (sto:path-scoped-projection) — nested entry points generated from the binding index plus host rule shims, never hand-written, always verified. M3b (sto:standard-check-declarations) — a standard declares its own checks, which turns a documented standard into an enforced one. M4 (sto:retrieval-surface-budget) — the retrieval surface stays one door: eka context plus --for, the MCP tool grouping the internal research already designed, and no twenty-sixth tool.","outOfScope":"RAG or vector search as a canonical retrieval path (deterministic graph retrieval already wins for constraint tracing; semantic search stays an optional non-canonical plugin). A large or LLM-generated AGENTS.md (the 2026 evidence measures context files lowering task success in 5 of 8 settings and raising cost by 20-23 percent). Hand-written nested entry points (N copies is block duplication; they must be generated and verified). New token families, spec-as-source, and large multi-agent orchestration (their failure patterns are already recorded). Server-side session state. A compliance gate measured in tokens. Enforcing non-mechanical standards such as clean architecture: those stay review checklists injected as prompt context, not gates."}